- _get_response: Yes, this function is on the call stack and orchestrates the call that leads to the error. It correctly identifies that the view has an async method (`post`) and wraps the view call in `async_to_sync`. This wrapper then attempts to run the view's `dispatch` method as a coroutine. The error occurs inside this `async_to_sync` wrapper when the `dispatch` method returns a non-awaitable object for the GET request.

